omx-plugins (0.21.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * strip-bands: the strip before its band count includes a moved header from
    its home
  * meter-held: the self-test copies a release tarball without git
  * descriptors: every link is at omx-dsp 0.34.2, the release installed
  * release: the zynthian bundle waits for debs that were built, not skipped
  * release: a devel push's qualify job reads the staging channel its build
    was staged to
  * contract directory: no schema-major level, the omx-plugins package is
    <contractdir>/omx-plugins (omx-contract 0.23.0)
  * domains: every domain is at 0.1.0, its vocabulary own version, never the
    package one
  * ci: the lint job folded from #214 keeps its runner and its steps key
  * release: a merge to devel publishes the real package to staging
  * deps-check.sh: its header names this repository's issue, not a private
    one (#221)
  * round-trip ledger: clap controls[].meaning loses 8 words, the four more
    being omx-glue's ratio, attack and release choices and omx-spring's
    damping in Hz
  * round-trip ledger: lv2 controls[].meaning loses 121 words, the five more
    being the new ceiling, damping, makeup, range and width
  * A drafted declaration marks its category for review, and the selftest
    settles it; the schema keeps its own layout
  * commit-msg: the hook is the shared stub, byte for byte
  * Presets and hints follow dBPerS; a fully hidden remote-controls page is
    not served, as #212 ruled, and the check says so (#221)
  * declarations: glue, upward, plosive, clipper and spring declare a panel
    family and its roles
  * declarations: each plugin states its category, as the owner ruled on
    2026-11-25
  * declaration: every plugin declares its category, and every shipped one a
    panel family
  * dBPerS: the balancer's and the leveler's Speed carry their unit and code
    (plugin-db's dBPerS); the folded leaves' tests agree on one tree (#221)
  * The labels domain is installed as omx-plugins', and the declaration
    schema's two last references name a document, no host (#221)
  * descriptor: typedBand's comment names its limit, the first run of digits
    (#218)
  * descriptor: the filter responses are read when a control states one,
    never at import (#218)
  * tests: a schema with no filterResponse stops only a control that states a
    response (red, #218)
  * recipes: parameters are by reference, whatever release is installed (#221)
  * No hand-kept floors: our packages are named without a version, a link's
    release is the installed owner's, requires is a list of names
  * descriptors: a choice's unit is the descriptor's choiceUnits, by the
    control's name, never an option beside it (omx-panel#68)
  * Fold repair: the pins route devel retired (#211) stays retired; the help
    names the curve proof
  * descriptors: an EQ states the response of its fixed filters, a word of
    the schema's filterResponse (#218)
  * tests: an EQ descriptor states the response of its fixed filters, and
    none on a typed band (red, #218)
  * Fold repair: make test runs meter-held and meter-rows (#206), and gen.mjs
    imports the format tables once (#200)
  * every control states its meaning, and the renderer refuses one that
    states none
  * tools/meanings.mjs: the table of each control's role, its listing and its
    apply
  * role-meanings: every role a word, never unknown; utility's speed and
    slope from omx-panel
  * docs: every control states its meaning, a role's or its own; enabled is
    no declared port's designation
  * ci: spdx-check and private-refs-check run in a lint job, never before
    make test
  * Language packs: the house fill job, and the catalogs where it reads them
  * contract-union: the stand-in install script places a domain as the real
    one does
  * round-trip: LV2 unit losses keyed by the PARAM_UNITS id, none and dBPerOct
  * round-trip-loss-units: the ledger's unit keys are PARAM_UNITS ids a
    descriptor states (red)
  * param contract: omx-balancer v4 and omx-loudlevel v3 for speed in dBPerS
  * meter ring: the policy masks carry 64 values
  * ci: make selftest runs as shards packed by measured time, today one under
    45 minutes
  * test: make selftest runs as CI shards under a 45-minute budget, every
    part in one (red)
  * curve-proof: omx-comp and omx-eq mark their curve `basis: exact`, and the
    measurement holds it
  * test-split lists plugin-labels among make test's checks
  * Section titles, choice labels and preset names get keys and catalogs;
    parameter names stay English
  * descriptors: every meter states held, clip and measurement
  * faces hold their meters until read, with the host's held and clip flags
  * N1: a plugin declares its own units in its declaration's `units` block
  * own-units: a declaration's own units, held over a fixture plugin (red)
  * meter ring: a clear ends every hold
  * format-tables: the lv2:designation row's pairs are plugin-db's meaning
    urns
  * format-tables: knee and makeup want the urn plugin-db declares for them
    (red)
  * meter ring: a take restarts the values it took, no others
  * meter ring: the held accumulator, the clip word and the read counter
  * declaration schema: reach omx-panel's definitions by the document name
    panel.schema.json
  * test: the declaration schema reaches omx-panel's definitions by document
    name (red)
  * clap-ext-check: the remote-control pages are the face's fixed cut, a
    hidden control's slot blank
  * release.yml: no dispatch publish input; the release jobs publish on a tag
    push alone
  * clap-probe: value_to_text's unit is held to the declared id's x-symbol
  * C2: every unit the tree states is the PARAM_UNITS id; a face shows the
    x-symbol
  * role-meanings-source-check: the scratch contract directory carries the
    installed domains
  * ci, release: each Fedora job runs one container per cell from
    check-matrix and release-matrix (#54)
  * lint: the shared fedora-cells check holds every workflow job to
    check-matrix's cells (red, #54)
  * debt growth: fetch the base into a private ref, and refuse a base that is
    HEAD (#102)
  * debt-base: the base fetch must leave the checkout's refs alone, and HEAD
    is no base (red, #102)
  * band-groups: a group is its plugin's URI by its symbol, and no two
    bundles state one node (#100)
  * band-groups: a group renamed into another plugin's namespace must go red
    (red, #100)
  * floors: plugin-hostd-contract >= 0.22.0 and plugin-db-contract >= 0.5.1,
    the tables format-tables reads (#182)
  * format-tables: the tables as x-kind map items, unit and meaning pairs
    read from their owners (#182)
  * test: format-tables reads the x-kind map tables and the owners' unit and
    meaning pairs (red, #182)
  * make docs-site and docs.yml: the per-plugin parameter reference published
    per release under /reference/omx-plugins/ (Open-Mixer/.github#242)
  * declaration schema: reach omx-panel's definitions by the document name
    panel.schema.json (#183)
  * test: the declaration schema reaches omx-panel's definitions by the
    document's name (red, #183)
  * docs: the format tables are x-kind map items, the unit and meaning pairs
    read from their owners (#182)
  * ci: an omx package from any repository but the channel's is refused,
    testing included (#56)
  * ci: the staging guard is one script, its self-test plants the release
    package's testing repositories (red, #56)
  * test-split: release-same-pass is listed among make test's prerequisites
    (#178)
  * no-host-nproc: a directory with no workflow is refused (exit 2), never
    passed (#63)
  * test: no artifact outlives 2 days off a release run, held by make test
    (#53)
  * packaging: the spec's CLAP floor is debian's, clap-devel >= 1.2.10 (#16)
  * deps-check: the spec's clap-devel floor must be debian's clap-headers
    floor (red, #16)
  * floors: omx-dsp-devel and omx-dsp-contract >= 0.34.1, the release with
    accel in coef
  * gen: the generated faces carry 0.21.0, the release bcb2d4c8 moved to
  * omx-rotary: accel travels in coef, not "x" (omx-contract 3.22.0)
  * release: the version moves to 0.21.0 (chain 3)
  * V23d: the omx-clap floor is 0.35.0, chain 3's omx-clap release
  * V23d: the old-include walk runs at the check's top level and sees the
    quoted include
  * V23d: red first, the old-include walk must see the quoted include too
  * V23d: the omx-clap floor is 0.36.0, the release that carries the domain
    omx-param-contract
  * V23d: oldUnitIncludes walks the tree for an include of omx-contract's old
    unit header
  * V23d: red first, make units refuses any file that includes omx-contract's
    old unit header
  * V23d: the unit codes are read from omx-clap's domain omx-param-contract
    and its render; the floor is omx-clap 0.35.0
  * V23d: red first, param-units-check reads the unit codes where omx-clap
    declares them
  * Contract files keep the $schema the floor's reader reads
  * The organisation's name: FreeMixer becomes Open-Mixer and OpenMixer
  * ci: the staging channel out again: an ordinary run builds against the
    channel (D25)
  * ci: staging back on the channel steps once more, so the guard fires now
    the build resolves (red, D25)
  * ci: the staging channel out again: an ordinary run builds against the
    channel (D25)
  * ci: every omx package comes from the channel, refused from staging;
    staging added back to show it fire (red, D25)
  * release: the same-pass list reaches every shared build call
  * deps-check: read a rich-form relation's name past its leading paren
  * deps-check: refuse a relation only to one of our names
  * deps-check: refuse any Breaks, Conflicts, Replaces, Obsoletes or Provides
  * Makefile help: panel-abi-refuses is part of make test and test-faces
  * panel-abi refuses by name when omx-clap-core's header is absent
  * tests: panel-abi must refuse by name when the clap-core header is absent
    (red)
  * round-trip: the losses ledger is generated from the run, with a drift
    check
  * panel-check: every meter a display reads is one the built face serves
  * probe-checks: a display reading a meter the built face does not serve
    goes red (red)
  * test-split: make test's new prerequisite, test-no-host-nproc, is listed
  * ci: heavy steps size their parallel jobs by the jobs action, never nproc
    (#63)
  * test: no workflow sizes its jobs from the host's nproc, red first (#63)
  * Artifact retention: pull-request and lane runs keep 2 days, release runs
    keep their value
  * deps-check: clap-devel's floor and ceiling follow clap-headers' (#16)
  * packaging: the rpm spec's clap-devel floor follows debian's, 1.2.10 (#16)

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:43:45 +0000
